// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
// kernel/user/store.fi -- THE STORE WINDOW (DAILY-DRIVER, roadmap r54 / P-007; redesign 11.10.2026).
//
//     store                 the window
//     store --list          no window: the catalog the provider returns, one line per program
//
// A native fUi program on the scene tree (fuiscene). It owns no rights and no
// network code: it asks the root provider `stored` over the action bus --
// store.list / store.status (reads), store.refresh (fetch the signed catalog),
// store.install / store.update / store.remove (critical: the broker asks, this
// window puts the question to the person -- the bundle is one the image ships, so
// its calls are the signed-in person's own). WHO MAY install or remove is decided
// by the provider from /etc/store.conf; the buttons here only follow its answer
// (`can_install`, `can_remove`). Nothing about that changed in the redesign.
//
// THE LOOK (Windows 11 Store feeling, own identity): a header card with the search box and
// the refresh button, a navigation column at the left (All, Programs, Themes, Fonts and media,
// Updates, Installed), a grid of cards (picture, name, one line of text, size, button) with
// pages, a detail page (big picture, text, version, size, source, check, buttons, progress
// bar), the updates list with "update all", and clean empty states (no hits, all current,
// no connection with a retry) plus a skeleton while the catalog loads.
//
// Keys: Ctrl+F search, Down from the search box into the grid, arrows move over the cards,
// PgUp / PgDn turn the page, Enter opens the detail page (or presses the focused button),
// Esc goes back (or clears the search), F5 / r fetch the catalog again, Tab walks everything.
// Every control has a name for the accessibility tree (the node's text, or a name of its own).
profile app

import ulib
import fuiscene
import fuiapp
import wlib
import actcli
import fui.grid

export { u_start }

